## Phase 5 — Upgrade Intent Classifier to Gemini (Excellence Boost)

> **Optional but high impact** — this closes the real accuracy gap honestly.

The current regex classifier achieves ~44.5% intent accuracy. An LLM-based classifier using Gemini can realistically reach **80–90%** which matches the historical numbers in the report.

#### [NEW] [`src/gemini_classifier.py`](file:///e:/Reply_agent/src/gemini_classifier.py)
A new classifier that:
1. Takes `(customer_message, prior_context)` as input
2. Sends a structured prompt to `gemini-2.5-flash` with the 8-intent taxonomy + few-shot examples
3. Returns `{intent, risk_signals, confidence}` as JSON
4. Falls back to regex rules if LLM call fails (maintaining reliability)

